## How sure are we?

- **Who to target is robust.** The model ranks churners well (ROC-AUC {{ model.selected_test.roc_auc | num(2) }}) and its probabilities are within {{ (model.selected_test.ece * 100) | num(1) }} points of observed churn. With all assumptions drawn at once, expected-value targeting beats risk-only in {{ mc.base_vs_risk.prob_gain | pct(0) }} of draws.
- **How much an offer saves is not.** Lists break even at a save rate of {{ be | pct }} (base budget) and {{ rbe | pct }} (recommended); we assume {{ default_offer.save_rate | pct(0) }}. Only {{ reasons.addressable_share | pct(0) }} of churners left for price or a competitor's offer, so {{ default_offer.save_rate | pct(0) }} means keeping {{ (default_offer.save_rate / reasons.addressable_share) | pct(0) }} of those an offer can reach.
- **Downside:** the recommended list loses money in {{ mc.recommended.prob_loss | pct(0) }} of draws{% if mc.recommended.p05 < 0 %}, and in the worst 5% it loses more than {{ (-mc.recommended.p05_scaled) | usd }} across the base{% endif %}; the smaller base-budget list loses in {{ mc.base.prob_loss | pct(0) }}.

## Risks and guardrails

- **No causal evidence yet.** Save rates are assumptions and contact can even raise churn, so the pilot keeps a random control group.
- **Sample data.** Real operators lose far fewer customers than this sample's {{ data.churn_rate | pct(0) }}. At {{ stress.targets[0] | pct(0) }} average churn only {{ s15.positive_ev_share | pct(0) }} of customers would be worth this offer, so offers and contact must get cheaper (for example SMS); retrain on our own data ([Vietnam deployment note](../docs/deployment-vietnam.md)).
- **Fairness.** Seniors are contacted {{ senior.ratio_to_reference | ratio(1) }} as often as others ({{ senior_risk.ratio_to_reference | ratio(1) }} under today's rule), {{ senior.risk_adjusted_ratio | ratio(1) }} after adjusting for risk. Age and gender are not model inputs; Legal/DPO reviews each wave.
- **Compliance.** Consent, Do-Not-Call checks, contact limits and a data-protection impact assessment.

## Decisions requested

1. **Approve one pilot wave:** {{ pilot.arm_size_per_wave | num }} customers offered, {{ pilot.arm_size_per_wave | num }} held out; offer and contact cost about {{ pilot.wave_cost | usd }}, expected net value of the offered half {{ pilot.wave_expected_net | usd }}, worst case (no one saved) {{ (-pilot.wave_cost) | usd }}.
2. **Name owners:** Retention (offers), Call centre (capacity), Finance (margin, offer cost), Legal/DPO (consent, DPIA).
3. **Agree the rule now:** after {{ pilot.outcome_window_days }} days, **go** if the effect is statistically significant and at least {{ rbe | pct }}; **stop** if clearly below; otherwise extend, at most {{ cfg.project.max_extend_waves }} more waves. At a true save rate of {{ default_offer.save_rate | pct(0) }} the rule says go {{ pilot.at_assumed.p_go | pct(0) }} of the time. Decision about {{ pilot.weeks_to_decision }} weeks after approval.
